### Assignment Objective:

In this assignment, you will work with the Chinook database to build and interact with a web API using ASP.NET Core. 
The goal is to gain hands-on experience developing a backend application that exposes data through structured endpoints, 
allowing you to practice routing, model binding, LINQ queries, and proper use of HTTP responses with using a database.

This assignment will be leaving more to you to piece together the solutions rather than having a tighter walk-through of the setup.

-----

### Setup

Create the project in the terminal:

    dotnet new mvc -o Martinka_ChinookEndpoints

Install the following in the terminal:

    // Dotnet EF Core Tool (Globally)
    dotnet tool install --global dotnet-ef

    // Dotnet ASP.NET Code Generator (Globally)
    dotnet tool install --global dotnet-aspnet-codegenerator

    // Dotnet VS Code Generation Design (Within the Project)
    dotnet add package Microsoft.VisualStudio.Web.CodeGeneration.Design

    // Dotnet - EF Core Tools (Within the Project)
    dotnet add package Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Design
    dotnet add package Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Tools
    dotnet add package Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Sqlite

    // Dotnet - Swagger (Within the Project)
    dotnet add package Swashbuckle.AspNetCore

*Properties* > *launchSettings.json*, update the following:

    "applicationUrl": "http://localhost:5000"

*Program.cs* > Before the **var app = builder.Build();** line and after **builder.Services.AddControllersWithViews();** line:

    // Provides endpoint metadata
    builder.Services.AddEndpointsApiExplorer();

    // Generates Swagger docs + UI
    builder.Services.AddSwaggerGen();
​
*Program.cs* > After your **var app = builder.Build();** line (*only to be used in development*):

    // Configure the HTTP request pipeline.
    if (!app.Environment.IsDevelopment()) {
        app.UseExceptionHandler("/Home/Error");
        // The default HSTS value is 30 days. You may want to change this for production scenarios, see https://aka.ms/aspnetcore-hsts.
        app.UseHsts();

    // Add this else to have these lines only occur during development.
    } else {
        // Generates swagger.json
        app.UseSwagger();
        // Serves the Swagger UI at /swagger
        app.UseSwaggerUI();
    }

